00:17:59.350 --> 00:17:59.970
but I know...

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:05.410
you're getting on my nerves you were only supposed to be here a couple of days jack i haven't been

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:16.710
here so long oh no when you first came here you had hair that's because i worry so much about your

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:22.670
lovely aunt sudie you see she's been ill and she hears you haven't been nice to me she'll be upset

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:29.980
All right, but Phil, you've got to make...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.800
some context.

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:32.360
You've got to do something

00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:33.020
for yourself.

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.020
You've got to make friends.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:40.040
At least he took my advice

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:41.160
about making friends.

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:42.860
Night after night,

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:43.440
they were there.

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:46.520
All right, Charlie,

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:47.440
I bet $200.

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:48.220
You in?

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:49.580
Phil, you were cleaned out

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:50.080
last night.

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:51.080
Where'd you get all this money?

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:51.780
I don't know.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:52.580
I found one of those

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:53.580
old things around the house.

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:54.400
You know, one of these things,

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:55.020
what do you call them?

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:56.260
Sold them to some jerk

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:57.360
for 75 bucks.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:18:59.780
Stradivarius, Stradivarius.

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:05.960
Hey, Jack, get that door, will you?

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:08.480
All right, I want... How many cars?

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:08.740
Three.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:09.700
Three? Yeah.

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:12.840
You? I'll take three, all right?

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:13.180
Good.

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:20.680
Why didn't my key work?

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:22.200
I had the lock change.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:24.440
Come on, Charlie.

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:29.840
Well, Phil, aren't you going to say hello?

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.180
Hello, hello, hello.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:32.120
All right, go.

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:34.310
We'll be here all day.

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:35.170
You in?

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:35.860
Okay.

00:19:36.630 --> 00:19:38.410
Is this the way to say hello to this lady?

00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:41.010
I never saw this lady before in my life.

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:41.650
But what do you want?

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:42.270
What?

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:43.020
Will you?

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:43.500
Will you?

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:44.740
Don't sit there like a clown.

00:19:44.900 --> 00:19:45.180
Will you?

00:19:47.220 --> 00:19:49.780
Oh, you never saw this lady in your life?

00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:50.260
No.

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:53.420
Well, Phil, I have news for you.

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:56.090
This lady is Aunt Sudie.

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:03.260
Remember, Sudie and the chicken soup?

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:06.450
Well, my glasses must have got misty again.

00:20:07.490 --> 00:20:08.590
Got a note on you.

00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:11.910
Who doesn't care about your note?

00:20:12.030 --> 00:20:12.650
Who's he?

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:14.190
I'll explain it to you later.

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:15.950
All right, Bill.

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:17.410
You stayed here long enough.

00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:17.990
Now, come on.

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:18.330
Out.

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:19.350
Out of this house.

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:20.070
Well, wait a second, Jack.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:20.910
I got three keys.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.210
I don't care what you're talking about.

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:22.890
Now, get out.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:23.950
Out of this house.

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:24.450
Go on.

00:20:24.670 --> 00:20:24.930
Out.

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:27.150
Jack, you're right to be upset and angry at me,

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:29.530
but don't humiliate me in front of my friends.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:31.680
Let me go out of here in my own way.

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:32.670
With dignity.

00:20:33.110 --> 00:20:34.270
All right, go with dignity.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:57.700
That was my introduction to Phil Silver.

00:20:58.820 --> 00:20:59.960
I finally got rid of him.

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:03.990
But my Aunt Sudie stayed for the next 12 years.

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:14.790
We'll be back in just a moment.

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:22.150
Thank you very much, ladies and gentlemen.

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:23.890
I hope you all enjoyed the show.

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:27.630
And I also want to thank my guest star, Phil Silver.

00:21:36.840 --> 00:21:42.020
You know, Silvers, Phil Silvers, isn't the only one that helped get started in show business.

00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:49.500
They helped Bob Hope, Ed Wynn, Weber and Fields, Sir Harry Lauder, John Wilkes Booth.

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:53.160
Well, I didn't exactly help John Wilkes Booth.

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:56.020
He just asked me if he could stay over to my house for a few days.

00:21:56.820 --> 00:21:58.740
Not that I know he was hiding out.

00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:02.880
Good night, folks. I'll be seeing you soon.

00:22:03.660 --> 00:22:28.340
At Comedy Central, we've got

00:22:28.390 --> 00:22:29.810
That Girl Starring

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:34.820
Thomas as Anne-Marie, a young actress trying to make him a big city without

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:37.480
sleeping her way to the top much.
